  schemaJson={JSON.stringify(schema)}
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 text-slate-200">
    <nav class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-emerald-400">Home</a> &gt; 
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-emerald-400">Patterns</a> &gt; 
      <span class="text-slate-400">RFC 5424 Syslog Grok Cheatsheet</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-10">
      <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/30 text-cyan-400 rounded-full text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider">
        Log Engineering Standard
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white mt-4 tracking-tight leading-tight">
        Syslog RFC 5424 Grok Pattern Validator &amp; Field Dictionary: Logstash, Vector &amp; Fluent Bit
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 mt-3 text-sm font-mono">
        IETF RFC 5424 Formal Standard • Ingestion Benchmarks • Updated September 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Quick Answer Callout: Exactly 48 words, bolded, theme accent border -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900/60 p-6 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-cyan-500 mb-10 text-slate-200">
      <p class="font-bold text-white mb-1">Quick Answer for Observability Engineers:</p>
      <p>
        The standardized production Grok regex for Syslog RFC 5424 across Logstash and Vector is: <code>^&lt;%&#123;POSINT:pri&#125;&gt;%&#123;NONNEGINT:ver&#125; +(?:%&#123;TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:ts&#125;|-) +(?:%&#123;HOSTNAME:host&#125;|-) +(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:app&#125;|-) +(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:proc&#125;|-) +(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:msgid&#125;|-) +(?:(?&lt;sd&gt;\[[^\]]+\])|-) *(?&lt;msg&gt;.*)$</code>. It handles mandatory nil-value hyphens (<code>-</code>) and fractional microsecond timestamps without catastrophic regular expression backtracking across distributed enterprise pipelines.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        IETF RFC 5424 Formal Specification vs. Legacy RFC 3164 BSD Syslog
      </h2>
      <p>
        For over two decades, enterprise log telemetry struggled under the ambiguities of the legacy <strong>RFC 3164 BSD Syslog protocol</strong> (published in 2001 as an informational summary of existing 1980s UNIX syslog behaviors). Under RFC 3164, timestamps omitted the year, lacked timezone offset notation, and provided zero standardization for process IDs or application identifiers. Downstream parsing systems were frequently forced to deploy brittle heuristic regular expressions that broke whenever hostnames contained hyphens or dates shifted across month boundaries.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) resolved these architectural deficiencies by establishing <strong>RFC 5424</strong> as the proposed standard. RFC 5424 fundamentally transforms syslog into a structured wire format by mandating:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Deterministic Header Ordering</strong>: An 8-field preamble consisting of PRI, VERSION, TIMESTAMP, HOSTNAME, APP-NAME, PROCID, MSGID, and STRUCTURED-DATA.</li>
        <li><strong>High-Resolution ISO-8601 Timestamps</strong>: Mandatory four-digit calendar years, millisecond or microsecond fractions, and explicit UTC or time zone offsets (e.g., <code>2026-09-24T18:45:00.123456+00:00</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Standardized Nil-Value Semantics</strong>: A uniform ASCII hyphen (<code>-</code>) representing omitted or inapplicable header attributes, eliminating guesswork in downstream indexing engines.</li>
        <li><strong>First-Class Structured Metadata</strong>: Enclosed bracket blocks allowing microservices, firewalls, and audit daemons to emit namespaced key-value parameters without polluting the human-readable payload string.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        In addition to payload formatting, RFC 5424 operates in conjunction with companion transport layer specifications. While RFC 5426 defines unencrypted transmission over UDP port 514 (subject to silent packet drop and maximum 2,048-byte truncation), enterprise architectures mandate <strong>RFC 5425 (TLS Transport Mapping over TCP port 6514)</strong> with mutual X.509 certificate validation. 
      </p>
      <p>
        Crucially, stream transmission over raw TCP introduces message boundary ambiguities. Under <strong>RFC 6587</strong>, syslog streaming over TCP supports two framing mechanisms: <em>non-transparent framing</em> (using newline <code>\n</code> delimiters) and <em>octet counting framing</em> (prefixing the log with its exact byte length, e.g. <code>184 &lt;165&gt;1 ...</code>). Non-transparent newline framing catastrophically fractures multi-line Java, Go, or Python stack traces into dozens of corrupted log entries. Production log forwarders (Vector and Fluent Bit) must always be configured with octet counting framing enabled to preserve multi-line trace integrity.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        The 8-Field Anatomy of an RFC 5424 Header: PRI, VERSION &amp; Fractional Timestamps
      </h2>
      <p>
        Consider a production Kubernetes ingress security event emitted over RFC 5424:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;165&gt;1 2026-09-24T14:32:10.987654+00:00 k8s-node-04 ingress-nginx 8841 ID-403 [sec@18234 tenant="corp" client_ip="198.51.100.42" threat_score="94"] Access denied by WAF rule 88219
</code></pre>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-700 bg-slate-900/40 rounded-lg">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-slate-950 text-cyan-400 border-b border-slate-700">
              <th class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800">Field Name</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800">Specification Definition</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800">Nil Value Permitted?</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800">Sample Wire Value</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800">Grok Token Pattern</th>
              <th class="p-3">Vector VRL Syntax</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800 text-slate-300">
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">PRI (Priority)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Facility * 8 + Severity</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-rose-400">No</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">&lt;165&gt;</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">&lt;%&#123;POSINT:pri&#125;&gt;</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.facility, .severity</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">VERSION</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Protocol Version (always 1)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-rose-400">No</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">1</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">%&#123;NONNEGINT:ver&#125;</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.version</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">TIMESTAMP</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">ISO-8601 Microsecond UTC</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">2026-09-24T14:32:10.987Z</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:%&#123;TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:ts&#125;|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.timestamp</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">HOSTNAME</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">FQDN or IPv4/IPv6 address</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">k8s-node-04</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:%&#123;HOSTNAME:host&#125;|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.host</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">APP-NAME</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Originating daemon/binary</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">ingress-nginx</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:app&#125;|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.appname</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">PROCID</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Process identifier/thread</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">8841</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:proc&#125;|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.procid</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">MSGID</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Message catalog identifier</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono">ID-403</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:%&#123;NOTSPACE:msgid&#125;|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.msgid</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/50">
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white border-r border-slate-800">STRUCTURED-DATA</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">Bracketed [id key="val"]</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 text-emerald-400">Yes (-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs">[sec@18234 ...]</td>
              <td class="p-3 border-r border-slate-800 font-mono text-cyan-300">(?:(?&lt;sd&gt;\[[^\]]+\])|-)</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">.structured_data</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        The Priority (PRI) value encapsulates both the originating system component (Facility) and the operational urgency (Severity) within a single compact integer:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Facility Code (Bits 7..3)</strong>: Calculated via right bitwise shift: <code>facility = pri &gt;&gt; 3</code> (or integer division <code>pri // 8</code>). Standard codes range from 0 (kernel messages), 3 (system daemons), 4/10 (security/authorization), up to 16–23 (user-reserved <code>local0</code> through <code>local7</code> commonly mapped to custom microservice tiers).</li>
        <li><strong>Severity Level (Bits 2..0)</strong>: Extracted via bitwise AND masking: <code>severity = pri &amp; 0x07</code> (or modulo <code>pri % 8</code>). Codes span from 0 (Emergency - system panic), 1 (Alert - immediate action required), 3 (Error - runtime failure), 5 (Notice - normal significant condition), to 7 (Debug - verbose diagnostic traces).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For instance, a PRI of <code>&lt;165&gt;</code> decomposes as: <code>165 &gt;&gt; 3 = 20</code> (Facility <code>local4</code>) and <code>165 &amp; 7 = 5</code> (Severity <code>Notice</code>). Parsing engines must expose these as dedicated indexed integer fields to allow SecOps SIEM filters like <code>severity &lt;= 3 AND facility IN [4, 10]</code> without re-evaluating raw text strings.
      </p>

      <!-- Interactive Tool: RFC 5424 Syslog Parser & Grok Extractor -->
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Interactive RFC 5424 Syslog Parser &amp; Grok Regex Extractor
      </h2>
      <p>
        Paste any RFC 5424 syslog string below to test extraction and inspect real-time JSON field decomposition:
      </p>

      <div class="my-6 p-6 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl space-y-6">
        <div>
          <div class="flex justify-between items-center mb-1">
            <label class="text-xs font-mono uppercase text-slate-400">Raw RFC 5424 Syslog Input String</label>
            <div class="space-x-2">
              <button id="btn-sample-waf" type="button" class="text-xs px-2 py-1 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-cyan-300 rounded font-mono">Load WAF Log</button>
              <button id="btn-sample-nil" type="button" class="text-xs px-2 py-1 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-cyan-300 rounded font-mono">Load Nil-Values</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <textarea id="syslog-input" rows="3" class="w-full bg-slate-950 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-white font-mono text-xs focus:border-cyan-500 focus:outline-none">&lt;165&gt;1 2026-09-24T14:32:10.987654+00:00 k8s-node-04 ingress-nginx 8841 ID-403 [sec@18234 tenant="corp" client_ip="198.51.100.42"] Access denied by WAF rule 88219</textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 pt-2 border-t border-slate-800 text-center">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="block text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Parse Status</span>
            <span id="out-parse-status" class="text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400 font-mono mt-1 block">VALID RFC 5424</span>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="block text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Calculated Facility</span>
            <span id="out-calc-fac" class="text-sm font-bold text-cyan-400 font-mono mt-1 block">20 (local4)</span>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="block text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Calculated Severity</span>
            <span id="out-calc-sev" class="text-sm font-bold text-amber-400 font-mono mt-1 block">5 (Notice)</span>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
            <span class="block text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Structured Data</span>
            <span id="out-calc-sd" class="text-sm font-bold text-purple-400 font-mono mt-1 block">Present (1 block)</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <label class="text-xs font-mono uppercase text-slate-400 block mb-1">Parsed JSON Output Representation</label>
          <pre is:raw id="out-json-view" class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto">{}</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <script is:raw>
        const facilities = [
          "kernel", "user", "mail", "daemon", "auth", "syslog", "lpr", "news",
          "uucp", "cron", "authpriv", "ftp", "ntp", "security", "console", "solaris-cron",
          "local0", "local1", "local2", "local3", "local4", "local5", "local6", "local7"
        ];
        const severities = [
          "Emergency (0)", "Alert (1)", "Critical (2)", "Error (3)",
          "Warning (4)", "Notice (5)", "Informational (6)", "Debug (7)"
        ];

        function parseSyslog5424(raw) {
          const regex = /^<(\d+)>(\d+)\s+([^\s]+)\s+([^\s]+)\s+([^\s]+)\s+([^\s]+)\s+([^\s]+)\s+(\[[^\]]+\]|-)\s*(.*)$/;
          const match = raw.trim().match(regex);
          if (!match) {
            return null;
          }

          const pri = parseInt(match[1], 10);
          const facility = pri >> 3;
          const severity = pri & 7;

          return {
            priority: pri,
            facility_code: facility,
            facility_name: facilities[facility] || "unknown",
            severity_code: severity,
            severity_name: severities[severity] || "unknown",
            version: parseInt(match[2], 10),
            timestamp: match[3] === "-" ? null : match[3],
            hostname: match[4] === "-" ? null : match[4],
            app_name: match[5] === "-" ? null : match[5],
            proc_id: match[6] === "-" ? null : match[6],
            msg_id: match[7] === "-" ? null : match[7],
            structured_data: match[8] === "-" ? null : match[8],
            message: match[9]
          };
        }

        function updateSyslogView() {
          const raw = document.getElementById('syslog-input').value;
          const res = parseSyslog5424(raw);

          const statusElem = document.getElementById('out-parse-status');
          const facElem = document.getElementById('out-calc-fac');
          const sevElem = document.getElementById('out-calc-sev');
          const sdElem = document.getElementById('out-calc-sd');
          const jsonElem = document.getElementById('out-json-view');

          if (res) {
            statusElem.textContent = "VALID RFC 5424";
            statusElem.className = "text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400 font-mono mt-1 block";
            facElem.textContent = res.facility_code + " (" + res.facility_name + ")";
            sevElem.textContent = res.severity_code + " (" + res.severity_name.split(' ')[0] + ")";
            sdElem.textContent = res.structured_data ? "Present" : "Nil (-)";
            jsonElem.textContent = JSON.stringify(res, null, 2);
          } else {
            statusElem.textContent = "SYNTAX ERROR";
            statusElem.className = "text-sm font-bold text-rose-400 font-mono mt-1 block";
            facElem.textContent = "N/A";
            sevElem.textContent = "N/A";
            sdElem.textContent = "N/A";
            jsonElem.textContent = '{\n  "error": "Failed to match RFC 5424 grammar. Check PRI bracket or nilvalue hyphens."\n}';
          }
        }

        document.getElementById('syslog-input').addEventListener('input', updateSyslogView);
        document.getElementById('btn-sample-waf').addEventListener('click', function() {
          document.getElementById('syslog-input').value = '<165>1 2026-09-24T14:32:10.987654+00:00 k8s-node-04 ingress-nginx 8841 ID-403 [sec@18234 tenant="corp" client_ip="198.51.100.42"] Access denied by WAF rule 88219';
          updateSyslogView();
        });
        document.getElementById('btn-sample-nil').addEventListener('click', function() {
          document.getElementById('syslog-input').value = '<34>1 2026-09-24T15:10:00Z web-lb-01 auth-service - - - User logged out successfully';
          updateSyslogView();
        });
        updateSyslogView();
      </script>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Enterprise Grok Patterns: Logstash Joni vs. Oniguruma vs. PCRE2 Engine
      </h2>
      <p>
        The standard production regular expression for Logstash and Elastic Agent requires precise non-capturing groups to handle optional nil-value hyphens without causing catastrophic backtracking:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto"><code># Logstash Production RFC 5424 Grok Pattern
SYSLOG5424_BASE ^&lt;%{POSINT:syslog_pri}&gt;%{NONNEGINT:syslog_ver} +(?:%{TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:syslog_ts}|-) +(?:%{HOSTNAME:syslog_host}|-) +(?:%{NOTSPACE:syslog_app}|-) +(?:%{NOTSPACE:syslog_proc}|-) +(?:%{NOTSPACE:syslog_msgid}|-) +(?:(?&lt;syslog_sd&gt;\[[^\]]+\])|-) *(?&lt;syslog_msg&gt;.*)$
</code></pre>

